  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Yellappa vs The State Of Maharashtra on 29 August, 2024 Author: Sudhanshu Dhulia Bench: Sudhanshu Dhulia 1 In The Supreme Court Of India Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Appeal No(S). 1206/2024 Yellappa & Anr. A Versus The State Of Maharashtra & Anr. With Criminal Appeal No(S). 1207/2024 O R D E R",
    "facts": "1. The appellants in both these appeals have challenged criminal proceedings initiated against them by means of an FIR No.31/2019 dated 06.02.2019 by which offences have been registered against them punishable under Sections 26 (2) (i) and (iv), 27 (2) and 23 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 r/w 2.3.4 of the Food Safety and Standards Rules, 2011, and under Sections 30(2), 2, 3, 4, 59 (iv) of Food Adulteration (Maharashtra Amendment), Act, 1969 and under Sections 328 and 188 of Indian Penal Code.",
    "arguments": "Moreover, the learned counsel representing the State of Maharashtra, Shri Aditya Aniruddha Pande, in his usual fairness has also stated before this Court that the items recovered from the appellants vehicle were sent for chemical analysis and the report says that all which was added in the beetle nut was sugar saccharine. 4."
  },
